-- 98: Mid-Atlantic fishing rules (US plan step 4): Virginia, Maryland, Delaware, New Jersey, Pennsylvania, D.C.
-- Checked 2026-10-21 on each state's own pages / 2026 guides (links in source_url). eRegulations.com pages are the digests the Maryland, Delaware,
-- New Jersey and Pennsylvania agencies publish and link from their own sites (each page shows its "last updated" date).
-- A state rule is a normal fish_rules row whose `regions` holds the 2-letter state code. Needs setup/94 first (its check allows these codes).
-- Where a rule changes by season or by water the app can only show one number, so the STRICTER one is the size/bag and the note has the rest.
-- Not added (nothing readable and current on the state's own page): Virginia Chesapeake Bay striped bass dates, Maryland catfish other than channel,
-- Delaware walleye/catfish, New Jersey spotted seatrout and trout, D.C. striped bass and crappie. The app says "We don't have a <State> rule for this fish yet".
-- Insert only; no delete / drop.

insert into fish_rules (species, match, regions, min_in, max_in, measure, one_over, bag, release_only, closed, open_only, note, source_url, verified_on, active) values
-- ---------------- Virginia (VMRC saltwater sheet updated April 2026; DWR 2026 freshwater creel table) ----------------
